Flip side: LLMs have to be very explicitly told to code in "modern" .NET and C# due to lack of representation in the training set.Case in point: extension members from C# 14 is one that LLMs commonly stumble on and requires an explicit example.  It still sometimes says that this is not valid syntax.    extension(SomeType instance)
    {
        public OtherType DoSomething() { ... }
    }

Agents really struggle on this one for some reason.Even older releases have a few that I notice LLMs making mistakes on like use of `System.Threading.Lock` over `Object` when locking.

